# G3 CERTIFICATE -- FINAL FORM
#
# Claim: fabric.conservation (all 9 asserts of f_fabric_conservation.v)
# holds unboundedly under the harness's own assumes, certified by plain
# k-induction over a netlist whose asserts are guarded by a sticky
# assume-violation flag (b' = b & !sticky) plus the 910-clause PDR
# invariant injected as $assume cells.
#
# Why this is engine-independent: the proof below is base-case +
# induction-step in smtbmc/boolector.  No PDR, no fold, no abc run log.
# The invariant was MINED with abc pdr (once) from a no-fold AIG whose
# write_aiger -symbols names every latch, so every clause resolved
# against the netlist's own wires: 910/910 kept, 0 dropped
# (inject_assumes.py report) -- vs the committed 854-clause lane where
# the fold-retimed latch ordinals left 246/854 ambiguous and trace
# matching resolved 668/673 folded latches as ambiguous.
#
# Self-checking: if any clause were mistranslated, the base case would
# fail loudly (the invariant is checked against reachable states), and
# a wrong guard would break the base case of the unguarded asserts'
# semantics (see transform_guards.py sticky discussion).
#
# Pipeline (all under formal/g3-kinduction/):
#   flatten.ys -> g3_flat.il
#   transform_guards.py -> g3_flat_guarded.il   (sticky assume guard)
#   guarded_aig.ys -> guarded_aig.il + .aim     (sby's aig model recipe)
#   bake_constraints.py -> guarded_baked.aig    (C-outputs baked in)
#   yosys-abc "pdr -d" -> guarded_inv.pla       (910 clauses, named)
#   inject_assumes.py -> guarded_assumed.il     (this file's input)
[options]
mode prove
depth 12

[engines]
smtbmc boolector

[script]
read_rtlil guarded_assumed.il
prep -top f_fabric_conservation

[files]
guarded_assumed.il
